WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.270
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:06.540 --> 00:08.700
- Are you here for the job offer ceremony, too? - Yeah.

3
00:08.840 --> 00:10.880
Have you decided which department you want to join?

4
00:11.040 --> 00:13.750
- I'm hoping for PR. - I see.

5
00:22.810 --> 00:24.690
Excuse me, hold the elevator!

6
00:31.570 --> 00:33.400
Excuse me.

7
00:39.100 --> 00:40.540
Looking forward to working with you.

8
00:41.560 --> 00:43.370
Likewise.

9
01:04.100 --> 01:10.099
(6 Years Later)

10
01:10.100 --> 01:12.400
(Chikubeni Co., Ltd.)

11
01:12.480 --> 01:16.000
Is your calculator broken, Kanda-san?

12
01:18.370 --> 01:21.340
The settlement for this travel advance is off.

13
01:21.690 --> 01:23.750
That's the third time this month.

14
01:24.850 --> 01:25.850
Huh?

15
01:29.770 --> 01:30.770
That's weird.

16
01:31.690 --> 01:32.690
Oh, you're right.

17
01:33.070 --> 01:35.090
Don't "oh, you're right" me.

18
01:35.650 --> 01:36.800
Please fix it immediately.

19
01:36.850 --> 01:38.290
Have it done before you leave today.

20
01:38.850 --> 01:39.850
That is all.

21
01:40.350 --> 01:41.970
Ah, wait, hold on!

22
01:46.580 --> 01:47.860
Don't be so mad.

23
01:48.110 --> 01:49.310
So impatient.

24
01:50.000 --> 01:51.890
I'll fix it right now, just give me a sec.

25
01:53.510 --> 01:58.040
Let's see, travel advance, travel advance...

26
01:58.550 --> 01:59.550
First, right here.

27
02:09.010 --> 02:10.450
Just watching them makes me nervous.

28
02:11.090 --> 02:13.630
Ueno-san is really strict, isn't he?

29
02:14.490 --> 02:17.280
Everyone in Accounting is by-the-book, especially him.

30
02:17.370 --> 02:19.010
Ueno-san isn't the issue here.

31
02:19.870 --> 02:21.870
Don't you think Kanda-san is acting a bit strange?

32
02:23.140 --> 02:24.369
How so?

33
02:24.370 --> 02:25.930
We're talking about the Kanda-san here.

34
02:28.610 --> 02:31.310
He won the company sales competition in his second year.

35
02:34.670 --> 02:36.370
His numbers are always at the top.

36
02:37.290 --> 02:40.170
He's only in his twenties, and he's already a top contender for manager.

37
02:40.590 --> 02:41.590
I'll keep doing my best.

38
02:42.300 --> 02:43.300
Thank you, everyone.

39
02:46.150 --> 02:48.370
He normally never messes up his paperwork.

40
02:49.630 --> 02:51.666
Despite how he looks, he's actually super thorough.

41
02:51.690 --> 02:55.260
He is the ace of the Sales Department, after all.

42
02:55.570 --> 02:57.050
And yet...

43
02:57.950 --> 03:00.350
Whenever it comes to accounting, Ueno's always chewing him out.

44
03:00.360 --> 03:04.370
- And always over rookie mistakes, too. - What are you getting at?

45
03:04.510 --> 03:08.480
Well, maybe Kanda-san actually hates Ueno-san's guts,

46
03:08.520 --> 03:10.920
and he's messing up on purpose just to give him a hard time.

47
03:11.570 --> 03:13.490
Kanda-san would never do something like that.

48
03:14.990 --> 03:18.190
I won't let you slander my bias like that.

49
03:18.650 --> 03:20.870
Your bias? Hey, you never know.

50
03:20.910 --> 03:23.170
You're so annoying, you always... Oh.

51
03:25.770 --> 03:28.080
Shima-san, you can't expense this.

52
03:28.250 --> 03:30.010
And the purpose isn't stated clearly enough.

53
03:30.270 --> 03:31.590
Go read the company guidelines...

54
03:34.350 --> 03:35.470
Please.

55
03:36.690 --> 03:37.890
Right, I'm sorry.

56
03:40.910 --> 03:42.750
That's what you get for running your mouth.

57
03:44.530 --> 03:46.770
It's been three years since I transferred to Accounting.

58
03:47.040 --> 03:49.790
Before that, I used to be in Sales, too.

59
03:52.150 --> 03:55.230
Though at this point, practically no one remembers that.

60
03:55.440 --> 03:57.370
I'm an accountant through and through now.

61
04:19.620 --> 04:20.820
I'm ho...

62
04:26.450 --> 04:28.290
Not again...

63
04:30.740 --> 04:32.870
Hey, what do you think you're...

64
04:38.900 --> 04:40.880
Oh, welcome back.

65
05:41.460 --> 05:44.270
"You Should Be The One To Come Kiss Me"

66
05:44.900 --> 05:47.799
(Episode 1)

67
05:47.800 --> 05:48.800
Huh?

68
05:53.180 --> 05:57.140
What are you doing walking around like that?!

69
06:00.050 --> 06:01.050
Sorry, my bad.

70
06:01.160 --> 06:03.650
I didn't expect you back so soon.

71
06:04.770 --> 06:07.940
For starters, don't walk around butt naked in someone else's house!

72
06:08.100 --> 06:10.220
Being naked in someone else's place is the best part.

73
06:13.110 --> 06:14.110
Kanda.

74
06:16.500 --> 06:18.280
Seriously, knock it off.

75
06:23.810 --> 06:25.060
Fine, I get it.

76
06:25.840 --> 06:27.050
I'm sorry, okay?

77
06:32.890 --> 06:33.890
Ooh!

78
06:34.100 --> 06:35.680
You've got beer.

79
06:37.520 --> 06:39.849
Put your underwear on first!

80
06:39.850 --> 06:40.900
Okay!

81
06:48.710 --> 06:51.230
For the record, I'm gay.

82
06:53.220 --> 06:54.220
And as for...

83
06:54.540 --> 06:58.370
this straight guy who makes himself right at home in my apartment,

84
06:58.500 --> 06:59.970
he knows it, too.

85
07:10.630 --> 07:12.140
Ahh!

86
07:12.840 --> 07:15.780
Beer always tastes better when you buy it, Ueno.

87
07:20.550 --> 07:21.620
So good.

88
07:24.710 --> 07:26.110
Is that supposed to be a dig at me?

89
07:28.030 --> 07:29.030
It all started

90
07:29.480 --> 07:31.320
back when I was still in the Sales Department.

91
07:55.850 --> 07:56.850
Kanda.

92
07:58.640 --> 08:00.030
Still working late?

93
08:00.850 --> 08:01.850
Yeah.

94
08:04.030 --> 08:05.030
What about you?

95
08:05.760 --> 08:06.760
Forget something?

96
08:07.600 --> 08:08.600
No.

97
08:09.980 --> 08:11.840
I figured I'd just crash at the office.

98
08:13.060 --> 08:14.060
Huh?

99
08:14.640 --> 08:17.970
There's a power outage or short circuit at my building, or something.

100
08:19.400 --> 08:21.640
They're still inspecting it, so I can't go home.

101
08:23.880 --> 08:27.290
I was gonna crash at a friend's place, but his girlfriend's coming over.

102
08:33.230 --> 08:34.330
What about a hotel?

103
08:35.480 --> 08:36.990
That's a waste of money.

104
08:44.694 --> 08:45.950
Sorry, I got it dirty.

105
08:48.120 --> 08:49.120
It's fine.

106
08:56.260 --> 08:58.080
I should've bought a towel on the way here.

107
10:05.140 --> 10:07.140
Want to stay at my place?

108
10:07.880 --> 10:08.880
It's close by, anyway.

109
10:19.200 --> 10:21.860
After that, for some reason, he just latched onto me.

110
10:22.030 --> 10:25.260
Before I knew it, he was sleeping over at my place almost every week.

111
11:00.660 --> 11:01.660
Hey.

112
11:01.800 --> 11:04.850
Stop staring at me. You're way too close.

113
11:05.330 --> 11:06.330
Hmm?

114
11:07.240 --> 11:09.060
Oh, sorry.

115
11:15.460 --> 11:16.610
No, it's just...

116
11:18.170 --> 11:20.010
I think I see a gray hair.

117
11:21.470 --> 11:22.470
What?!

118
11:24.060 --> 11:25.060
Where?

119
11:25.700 --> 11:28.130
- Where is it? - Let me see.

120
11:28.400 --> 11:29.400
Huh?

121
11:35.650 --> 11:36.650
Whoa...

122
11:37.260 --> 11:38.810
There's a bunch of them.

123
11:40.010 --> 11:41.010
What?!

124
11:41.530 --> 11:42.650
You've got to be kidding me.

125
11:47.050 --> 11:48.830
Gotcha!

126
11:49.200 --> 11:51.970
Man, Ueno, you're way too gullible.

127
11:52.300 --> 11:53.300
I'm hitting the bathroom.

128
11:57.960 --> 11:59.010
Someone's at the door.

129
12:08.560 --> 12:09.560
Coming.

130
12:09.770 --> 12:11.480
Delivery from Yamaneko Express.

131
12:12.730 --> 12:13.730
Alright.

132
12:24.570 --> 12:27.200
Another package came for you.

133
12:28.870 --> 12:31.530
Oh right, I totally forgot. Thanks!

134
12:31.740 --> 12:32.980
Don't "thanks" me.

135
12:33.900 --> 12:35.000
Huh?

136
12:46.050 --> 12:49.030
I ordered this during a sale the other day.

137
12:49.520 --> 12:51.640
Why did you have it shipped to my place?

138
12:51.850 --> 12:54.330
I was gonna bring it over here anyway.

139
12:54.640 --> 12:55.640
Wanna play a game?

140
12:59.410 --> 13:00.420
Of course.

141
13:01.580 --> 13:03.710
If it weren't for you, I never would've bought it.

142
13:03.820 --> 13:05.200
I'd have no use for it.

143
13:07.070 --> 13:11.510
Kanda was like this even before I came out to him. He hasn't changed a bit.

144
13:18.840 --> 13:21.890
Hey, quit taking over my shelves without asking.

145
13:21.970 --> 13:23.576
What's the big deal? The space was empty anyway.

146
13:23.600 --> 13:25.170
It's called interior design, okay?

147
13:25.260 --> 13:26.870
Don't be so stingy.

148
13:26.920 --> 13:27.920
Just hold on a sec.

149
13:28.080 --> 13:29.716
I'll line up all the corners nice and neat for you.

150
13:29.740 --> 13:31.290
Lining up the corners isn't the point!

151
13:31.350 --> 13:32.818
Come on, I know how picky you are about details.

152
13:32.842 --> 13:34.346
If anything, he's only gotten pushier.

153
13:34.370 --> 13:35.730
What kind of idiot puts stuff right in front of the speaker?

154
13:35.740 --> 13:37.460
Who cares? They're both rectangular anyway.

155
13:37.700 --> 13:38.900
Just put it over here for now.

156
13:39.620 --> 13:42.000
You can't even see it there. That's no fun...

157
13:47.770 --> 13:50.030
You're off by a digit on the billing amount here, too.

158
13:50.950 --> 13:51.730
Sorry.

159
13:51.810 --> 13:52.910
Please fix it.

160
13:53.160 --> 13:54.616
Yes, sir! I'll have it fixed by the end of the week.

161
13:54.640 --> 13:55.640
By the end of the day.

162
13:57.790 --> 13:59.460
- Ah, Shirai-san. - Yes?

163
13:59.710 --> 14:01.710
- Here. - Oh, thank you.

164
14:03.710 --> 14:09.050
I'll stop by to visit you again next week.

165
14:09.330 --> 14:10.330
Sounds good.

166
14:10.800 --> 14:11.800
Thank you for your time.

167
14:13.110 --> 14:14.110
Kanda.

168
14:14.850 --> 14:15.850
Yes?

169
14:22.150 --> 14:26.130
Back again, Ueno? Accounting sure is tough.

170
14:26.470 --> 14:29.230
Mizoguchi, and Kobayashi. Long time no see.

171
14:29.370 --> 14:30.470
Long time no see.

172
14:31.280 --> 14:32.490
Rare to see you two paired up.

173
14:33.500 --> 14:36.490
The company newsletter is doing a feature on the new recruits in Sales.

174
14:36.790 --> 14:38.416
The section chief threw me under the bus.

175
14:38.440 --> 14:39.640
Let's make the headline,

176
14:40.000 --> 14:41.750
"The Next Ace of the Sales Department."

177
14:42.040 --> 14:44.190
"Leave the Numbers to Me!" How's that?

178
14:44.380 --> 14:45.380
Very funny.

179
14:46.280 --> 14:48.690
It's an honor to be in the newsletter.

180
14:50.890 --> 14:53.400
- Way to go! - Thank you!

181
14:54.260 --> 14:55.180
- Is it true? - Yeah!

182
14:55.180 --> 14:56.180
Whoa!

183
15:02.150 --> 15:05.430
Maybe a peace sign is a bit much. Thanks, everyone.

184
15:05.840 --> 15:07.410
Speak of the reigning ace of Sales.

185
15:08.120 --> 15:10.950
Kanda-senpai just landed the Lanau Corp contract!

186
15:11.690 --> 15:13.256
He actually closed the deal with Lanau Corp...?

187
15:13.280 --> 15:14.280
Yeah.

188
15:14.660 --> 15:17.540
That single deal just hit our department's target for the whole quarter.

189
15:17.870 --> 15:18.910
That's insane.

190
15:19.500 --> 15:20.950
Let's get him to treat us next time.

191
15:21.580 --> 15:22.850
Shouldn't we be treating him?

192
15:23.400 --> 15:25.670
Details, details.

193
15:51.240 --> 15:52.240
Yo!

194
16:03.250 --> 16:05.120
This one's going up.

195
16:05.590 --> 16:06.710
You could've told me sooner.

196
16:13.050 --> 16:15.390
Heard you landed the Lanau contract.

197
16:15.800 --> 16:18.140
Oh, word got around?

198
16:19.060 --> 16:22.190
I'm seriously carrying this company on my back, huh?

199
16:22.920 --> 16:26.810
So come on, Ueno, shower me with praise.

200
16:28.280 --> 16:29.280
Congrats.

201
16:36.030 --> 16:37.030
What the heck?

202
16:37.640 --> 16:39.720
You call that congratulating me?

203
16:41.160 --> 16:42.160
Con-grats.

204
16:42.370 --> 16:43.370
Just two syllables?

205
16:48.130 --> 16:53.140
Come on, even someone on the street would at least give me the full "congratulations"!

206
16:54.160 --> 16:56.890
Can't you put a little more effort into it?

207
16:57.020 --> 16:58.560
Fine, fine.

208
16:59.770 --> 17:01.220
Con-grat-u-la-tions.

209
17:02.580 --> 17:03.890
Zero emotion.

210
17:07.490 --> 17:08.580
Sorry, sorry.

211
17:10.980 --> 17:13.170
I really am happy for you, though.

212
17:21.010 --> 17:22.010
In that case,

213
17:22.240 --> 17:24.930
I'll send you my wish list in the next few days.

214
17:27.690 --> 17:28.690
Huh?

215
17:28.980 --> 17:30.080
Wish list?

216
17:32.490 --> 17:33.690
This is your floor, Ueno.

217
17:35.140 --> 17:36.140
Oh.

218
18:12.490 --> 18:13.890
Keep up the good work.

219
18:14.270 --> 18:16.650
[Kanda:] Here's that wish list I mentioned.

220
18:24.140 --> 18:26.580
It's nothing but cheap snacks.

221
18:32.610 --> 18:34.330
What goes on in that guy's head...

222
19:13.870 --> 19:14.870
Welcome.

223
19:32.580 --> 19:33.590
Would it be weird...

224
19:34.610 --> 19:37.960
to buy a tie for a friend?

225
19:40.900 --> 19:42.780
I'm really clueless about this kind of thing...

226
19:44.940 --> 19:45.940
Still,

227
19:46.570 --> 19:48.320
seeing how hard he works every day,

228
19:49.470 --> 19:51.830
makes me want to get him something special once in a while.

229
19:55.300 --> 19:56.300
I just want...

230
19:58.430 --> 20:00.380
to see an even bigger smile on his face.

231
20:10.670 --> 20:11.670
Excuse me.

232
20:44.830 --> 20:46.070
That was close.

233
20:48.290 --> 20:51.570
I almost got carried away again.

234
21:04.720 --> 21:06.390
I should just stick to the cheap snacks.

235
21:07.450 --> 21:09.260
He was just joking around anyway.

236
21:12.520 --> 21:14.560
If I do anything to ruin what we have now,

237
21:16.240 --> 21:17.240
I'm sure...

238
21:18.670 --> 21:20.310
he'll stop coming over altogether.

239
21:45.470 --> 21:46.800
I'm beat.

240
21:47.800 --> 21:50.200
Who calls at an hour like this?

241
21:53.230 --> 21:55.110
- Good work today. - You too.

242
21:58.400 --> 21:59.400
Got it.

243
22:01.730 --> 22:03.430
- Is something wrong? - Huh?

244
22:05.560 --> 22:06.560
Oh.

245
22:08.240 --> 22:09.240
It's nothing.

246
22:10.210 --> 22:11.410
"Nothing," huh...

247
22:29.380 --> 22:30.830
Don't say anything I shouldn't.

248
22:31.890 --> 22:33.090
Don't do anything I shouldn't.

249
22:37.640 --> 22:40.640
I've been letting him get too close lately.

250
22:42.010 --> 22:43.110
I need to be more careful.

251
22:50.340 --> 22:51.340
Ah!

252
22:56.420 --> 22:57.620
Shoot.

253
22:58.890 --> 23:00.200
Missed it.

254
23:20.130 --> 23:21.130
Hey.

255
23:21.630 --> 23:22.930
Can I come over tonight?

256
23:29.070 --> 23:30.270
Here we go again...

257
23:44.520 --> 23:47.040
(Next Episode Preview) Are you and Ueno-san close, Kanda-senpai?

258
23:47.260 --> 23:49.560
Didn't I tell you not to talk to me at work?

259
23:49.860 --> 23:51.400
Actually, I'm gay, too.

260
23:52.860 --> 23:54.420
Then can I come over to your place?

261
23:55.240 --> 23:56.720
Last time was just a coincidence.

262
23:57.040 --> 23:58.800
Kanda-san and I aren't actually that close.
